{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the probability that the product of the numbers on two fair 6-sided dice is a multiple of 5, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of possible outcomes**:\n   Each die has 6 faces, so there are \\(6 \\times 6 = 36\\) possible outcomes when two dice are thrown.\n\n2. **Determine the condition for the product to be a multiple of 5**:\n   The product of the numbers on the two dice will be a multiple of 5 if at least one of the dice shows a 5. This is because 5 is a prime number, and the only way to get a multiple of 5 from the product of two numbers is if at least one of those numbers is 5.\n\n","prefix_end":624,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,18927,429,279,1985,315,279,5109,389,1378,6624,220,21,49758,22120,374,264,5248,315,220,20,11,582,686,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,2790,1372,315,3204,19554,334,510,256,8886,2746,702,220,21,12300,11,773,1052,525,17767,21,1124,15136,220,21,284,220,18,21,57758,3204,19554,979,1378,22120,525,14989,382,17,13,3070,35,24308,279,2971,369,279,1985,311,387,264,5248,315,220,20,334,510,256,576,1985,315,279,5109,389,279,1378,22120,686,387,264,5248,315,220,20,421,518,3245,825,315,279,22120,4933,264,220,20,13,1096,374,1576,220,20,374,264,10250,1372,11,323,279,1172,1616,311,633,264,5248,315,220,20,504,279,1985,315,1378,5109,374,421,518,3245,825,315,1846,5109,374,220,20,382,18,13,3070,2507,279,1372,315,36749,19554,334,510,256,481,1416,279,1156,2746,4933,264,220,20,11,279,2086,2746,646,387,894,315,279,220,21,12300,13,1096,6696,601,220,21,19554,25,320,20,11,16,701,320,20,11,17,701,320,20,11,18,701,320,20,11,19,701,320,20,11,20,701,320,20,11,21,4292,256,481,1416,279,2086,2746,4933,264,220,20,11,279,1156,2746,646,387,894,315,279,220,21,12300,13,1096,6696,601,2441,220,21,19554,25,320,16,11,20,701,320,17,11,20,701,320,18,11,20,701,